  "body": "## Summary\n\nThis PR adds the **X-COM Serial2CAN bridge** in a new top-level `X-Verse/`\nfolder. The bridge connects serial-attached ECUs that speak the Lawicell\n**SLCAN** protocol, such as the ThreadX zonal ECU on the MXChip AZ3166, to an\nX-Verse CAN bus in both directions:\n\n- SocketCAN `vcan0`, the standard X-Verse setup\n- rootless `udp_multicast`\n\nOnce bridged, the unchanged Zenoh2CAN bridge, the VCU, the virtual vehicle,\nCARLA and tools like `candump` see the ECUs as ordinary CAN nodes.\n\n```text\nserial ECU \u2500\u2500SLCAN/UART\u2500\u2500 Serial2CAN \u2500\u2500 CAN bus \u2500\u2500 Zenoh2CAN (unchanged) \u2500\u2500 Zenoh \u2500\u2500 X-Verse / CARLA\n```\n\nCloses #17\n\n> **Stacked on #32.** The branch builds on `feature/threadx-zonal-architecture`\n> (AZ3166 firmware, `configure_bridge.py --bus-type`, live X-Verse test\n> script), so this PR targets that branch and shows only the bridge commit.\n> When #32 is merged and its branch deleted, GitHub retargets this PR to\n> `main`. Merge #32 first.\n\n## What's included (`X-Verse/bridges/serial2can/`)\n\n| Feature | Behaviour |\n| --- | --- |\n| Framing | Lawicell SLCAN `t`/`T`/`r`/`R` lines with a strict decoder: length, DLC, ID range, hex, optional timestamp |\n| Signal routing | Per-port `to_serial` and `from_serial` ID filters (`id`/`mask`/`extended`), JSON configuration |\n| Bidirectional | Serial \u2192 CAN, CAN \u2192 serial, and serial-to-serial fan-out (shared-bus semantics for several ECUs) |\n| Handshake | `C`, `V`, `S<n>`, `O` on every connect; the ECU's state frame after `O` is forwarded |\n| Interrupted links | Unplug and write failures are detected; the bridge reconnects with a fresh handshake; device paths can be globs (`/dev/serial/by-id/...`) |\n| Back-pressure | Bounded per-port queues; drops are counted, and the CAN loop never blocks |\n| `udp_multicast` | Echo guard stops looped-back frames from returning to their ECU |\n| Shutdown | `C` sent to every ECU on SIGINT/SIGTERM; the AZ3166 switches its lamps off |\n| Observability | Periodic JSON statistics per port |\n\nThe layout follows the other X-Verse bridges: `src/`, `config/` (`vcan0`,\n`udp_multicast` and a multi-ECU example), a `launch/bridge_launch.py` that\nprepares `vcan0`, `tests/`, a README and a PlantUML architecture diagram.\n\n## Verification\n\n- **302 host tests (pytest)** run with no hardware and no root:\n  - codec, filter, echo guard and config unit tests\n  - the real bridge against **simulated SLCAN ECUs on Linux pseudo-terminals**:\n    handshake, both directions, fan-out, unplug and replug, write failures,\n    non-tty and late devices, CAN send errors, FD and error frames, the CLI\n    lifecycle\n  - coverage: **95% line / 90% branch**\n  - ruff and mypy clean\n- **Physical AZ3166** (`tests/hardware_check.py`): 6/6 checks passed.\n  - All 256 status bytes through the bridge and ECU (median round trip\n    **4.9 ms**).\n  - Heartbeat forwarded at 0.994 s, the `to_serial` filter works, and SIGTERM\n    sends `C`.\n  - The ECU reports lamps off afterwards.\n  \u2192 [evidence/hardware-check](X-Verse/bridges/serial2can/evidence/hardware-check/results.json)\n- **Live X-Verse + CARLA** (`run_autoverse.py --enable-camera-display --vcu-zenoh`):\n  - Path: Manual Control keys \u2192 VCU \u2192 Zenoh2CAN (`udp_multicast`) \u2192\n    **Serial2CAN** \u2192 AZ3166 \u2192 back \u2192 CARLA.\n  - 6/6 steps matched the expected light states (8 / 0 / 64 / 72 / 64 / 0),\n    with VCU \u2192 CARLA lamp at most 59 ms.\n  - Rear-camera frames included.\n  \u2192 [evidence/xverse-carla](X-Verse/bridges/serial2can/evidence/xverse-carla/results.json)\n- **ASPICE SWE.1\u2013SWE.6** ([aspice/](X-Verse/bridges/serial2can/aspice/README.md)):\n  - requirements in Markdown, PlantUML architecture and design\n  - unit, integration and qualification specs\n  - an HTML report generator that re-runs the tests and checks that the\n    recorded evidence matches the current sources\n  - result: 19/21 requirements verified, 0 trace issues\n\n**Defects found and fixed during verification:**\n\n- tokens lost in the stream splitter during the handshake\n- under-counted disconnects after writer-detected link loss\n- test interference from a live `udp_multicast` bus on the same UDP port.\n  Linux delivers every group to all sockets on a port; this is documented in\n  the README.\n\n## Acceptance criteria (#17)\n\n- [x] **Agreed signal mapping is demonstrated:** the X-Verse lighting traffic\n  (`0x1F1` \u2192 ECU, `0x1F4`/`0x1F5` \u2192 bus) through per-port filters, on\n  hardware and in live X-Verse.\n- [x] **Malformed or unavailable inputs are handled:**\n  - malformed lines and BELL replies are counted\n  - FD and error frames are not forwarded\n  - missing, non-tty, unplugged and failing devices are retried without\n    affecting other ports\n- [x] **Build and configuration instructions are available:** see\n  [README](X-Verse/bridges/serial2can/README.md) (install, bus choice, run,\n  connect X-Verse, configuration reference, testing).\n\n## How to test\n\n```bash\ncd X-Verse/bridges/serial2can\npython3 -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install -r requirements-dev.txt\nPYTHONPATH= PYTEST_DISABLE_PLUGIN_AUTOLOAD=1 .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests     # 302 tests\n.venv/bin/python src/serial2can_bridge.py config/az3166-udp-multicast.json          # with the AZ3166 attached\n```\n\n## Known limitations and open items\n\n- **Not tested here:**\n  - SocketCAN `vcan0` (creating it needs root; same python-can path as\n    `udp_multicast`)\n  - two physical ECUs on one bus (the OpenBSW S32K148 firmware doesn't speak\n    SLCAN yet; fan-out is verified with simulated ECUs)\n- **Protocol limits:** SLCAN carries no CAN error frames or CAN FD, and the\n  bridge does not emulate bit timing or arbitration.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
